## manifest.json (aka App Descriptor)
JSON file describing:
- App metadata
- Data sources
- UI routing
- SAPUI5 dependencies
- Fiori launchpad integration

## Estructura
```json
{
    '_version': '1.32.0',
    'sap.app': {
        'id': 'com.empresa.miapp',
        'type': 'application',
        'title': '{{title}}',
        'description': '{{description}}',
        'i18n': 'i18n/i18n.properties',
        'applicationVersion': { 'version': '1.0.0' },
        'dataSources': {
            'mainService': {
                'uri': '/sap/opu/odata/sap/API_PRODUCT/',
                'type': 'OData',
                'settings': { 'odataVersion': '4.0' }
            }
        },
        'crossNavigation': {
            'inbounds': {
                'inbound1': {
                    'semanticObject': 'Product',
                    'action': 'display',
                    'signature': {
                        'parameters': { 'ProductID': {} }
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    },
    'sap.ui5': {
        'dependencies': {
            'minUI5Version': '1.120.0',
            'libs': {
                'sap.m': {},
                'sap.ui.core': {}
            }
        },
        'models': {
            'i18n': {
                'type': 'sap.ui.model.resource.ResourceModel',
                'settings': { 'bundleName': 'com.empresa.miapp.i18n.i18n' }
            },
            '': {
                'dataSource': 'mainService',
                'preload': true
            }
        },
        'routing': {
            'config': {
                'routerClass': 'sap.m.routing.Router',
                'viewType': 'XML',
                'viewPath': 'com.empresa.miapp.view',
                'controlId': 'app',
                'controlAggregation': 'pages'
            },
            'routes': [
                {
                    'pattern': '',
                    'name': 'main',
                    'target': 'main'
                },
                {
                    'pattern': 'product/{id}',
                    'name': 'detail',
                    'target': 'detail'
                }
            ],
            'targets': {
                'main': { 'viewName': 'Main' },
                'detail': { 'viewName': 'Detail' }
            }
        }
    },
    'sap.fiori': {
        'registrationIds': [],
        'archeType': 'transactional'
    }
}
```

## Secciones

### sap.app
- **id** — namespace único
- **type** — application, component, library
- **title / description** — i18n keys
- **dataSources** — OData/REST endpoints
- **crossNavigation** — inbound/outbound intents (launchpad)

### sap.ui5
- **dependencies** — SAPUI5 libs
- **models** — data + i18n models
- **routing** — URL patterns to views
- **rootView** — main view

### sap.fiori
- **archeType** — app category
- **registrationIds** — SAP registration

### sap.platform.cf (opcional)
- BTP-specific deployment settings

### sap.platform.abap (opcional)
- ABAP-specific settings

## Data source con destination
```json
'dataSources': {
    'mainService': {
        'uri': '/api/product/',
        'type': 'OData',
        'settings': { 'localUri': 'localService/metadata.xml' }
    }
}
```

Con xs-app.json routing, apunta a real destination.

## Fiori launchpad target
```json
'crossNavigation': {
    'inbounds': {
        'inbound1': {
            'semanticObject': 'Product',
            'action': 'display'
        }
    }
}
```

Users navigate via `#Product-display?ProductID=123`.

## Cambios comunes
- Add data source → agregar en `dataSources`
- New route → agregar a `routes`
- Change min UI5 version → `dependencies.minUI5Version`

## OData v2
SAP's initial standard. Widely deployed en ECC + older S/4HANA.

### Characteristics
- Metadata document (XML)
- URL patterns: `/EntitySet(key)`
- Query: `$filter`, `$orderby`, `$expand`, `$top`, `$skip`
- Batch: `$batch` endpoint

## OData v4
Modern standard. Native en S/4HANA Cloud, newer SAP products.

### Improvements over v2
- JSON payloads (more compact)
- Delta queries (efficient sync)
- Streaming
- Better navigation semantics
- More flexible querying (`$search`, `$apply`, `$compute`)

### Backward-incompatible
- URL syntax differences
- Metadata format changes
- Some annotations moved

## En Fiori
### Configure
manifest.json:
```json
'dataSources': {
    'mainService': {
        'uri': '/api/odata/',
        'type': 'OData',
        'settings': {
            'odataVersion': '4.0'
        }
    }
}
```

### Model class
- v2: `sap.ui.model.odata.v2.ODataModel`
- v4: `sap.ui.model.odata.v4.ODataModel`

## Consumo diferente en controller

### v2
```javascript
var oModel = this.getView().getModel();
oModel.read('/Products', {
    success: function(data) {
        // data.results = array
    }
});

// Create
oModel.create('/Products', { Name: 'X', Price: 100 }, {
    success: function(oData) { ... }
});

// Update
oModel.update('/Products(1)', { Price: 120 }, {
    success: function() { ... }
});
```

### v4
```javascript
var oModel = this.getView().getModel();
var oBinding = oModel.bindList('/Products');
oBinding.requestContexts().then(function(contexts) {
    // contexts array of Context objects
});

// Create
var oContext = oModel.bindList('/Products').create({ Name: 'X', Price: 100 });
await oContext.created();

// Update — via 2-way binding automatic
Input value change → oContext.setProperty('Price', 120);
// Auto-submitted or batched
```

v4 más 'reactive' — bindings automatically sync.

## $batch differences

### v2
Multiple ops in 1 HTTP request via `$batch` endpoint. Requires special MIME formatting.

### v4
Same endpoint but simpler JSON batch payload.

En v4, batch happens more transparently (framework handles).

## Migration v2 → v4
Si tu Fiori app está en v2 y backend switches to v4:
- Change model class
- Update controller code (bindings API changed)
- Test extensively

**No trivial**. Plan effort.

## Choosing version para new project
- **v4** if starting fresh + backend supports
- **v2** if backend is ECC / older S/4HANA sin v4 services

## Common issues
- **Metadata parse error** — mixing v2 metadata con v4 model
- **Filter syntax différente** — `substringof` (v2) vs `contains` (v4)
- **Function imports** — API changes

## Debugging
- Network tab en browser DevTools → see actual HTTP requests
- Enable UI5 diagnostics: `Ctrl+Alt+Shift+P`

## Intent-based navigation
Fiori launchpad usa 'intents' — semantic objects + actions.

### Semantic Object
Business concept (e.g., `Product`, `SalesOrder`).

### Action
Operation (e.g., `display`, `manage`, `create`).

### Ejemplo
`#Product-display?ProductID=123` — Product semantic object, display action, con ProductID param.

## Register app inbound
manifest.json:
```json
'crossNavigation': {
    'inbounds': {
        'inbound1': {
            'semanticObject': 'Product',
            'action': 'display',
            'signature': {
                'parameters': {
                    'ProductID': { 'required': true }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
```

Registered en launchpad (via administration).

## Navigate desde app A → app B
```javascript
var oCrossAppNavigator = sap.ushell.Container.getService('CrossApplicationNavigation');

oCrossAppNavigator.toExternal({
    target: {
        semanticObject: 'Product',
        action: 'display'
    },
    params: {
        ProductID: '123'
    }
});
```

## Get hash for links
```javascript
var sHash = oCrossAppNavigator.hrefForExternal({
    target: { semanticObject: 'Product', action: 'display' },
    params: { ProductID: '123' }
});
// Use en <Link href=sHash/>
```

## Back navigation
```javascript
oCrossAppNavigator.backToPreviousApp();
```

O browser back button.

## Cross-app messaging
Apps can share state via **AppState service**:
- App A saves state (session-scoped)
- App B loads state
- Efficient for large filters/selections

## Retain filters on navigate
Use `AppState` to persist filter values entre apps.

## Multi-context
User opens multiple apps → each keeps context.

## Deep linking
Bookmarkable URLs:
`https://launchpad/#Product-display?ProductID=123`

User reloads → same state.

## Common issues
- **'App not registered'** — inbound missing en manifest, o registration not done in launchpad
- **'Insufficient authorizations'** — user lacks role for target app
- **'Parameter missing'** — required signature parameter not passed

## Testing
En dev: BAS runs mini-launchpad (mock). Cross-nav works.
En prod: real launchpad.

## Roles + navigation
User sees only apps assigned to their role. Cross-nav fails silently if user has no access to target.

## Config routing
manifest.json:
```json
'sap.ui5': {
    'routing': {
        'config': {
            'routerClass': 'sap.m.routing.Router',
            'viewType': 'XML',
            'viewPath': 'com.empresa.miapp.view',
            'controlId': 'app',
            'controlAggregation': 'pages',
            'transition': 'slide'
        },
        'routes': [
            {
                'pattern': '',
                'name': 'list',
                'target': 'list'
            },
            {
                'pattern': 'detail/{productId}',
                'name': 'detail',
                'target': 'detail'
            },
            {
                'pattern': 'detail/{productId}/edit',
                'name': 'edit',
                'target': 'edit'
            }
        ],
        'targets': {
            'list': { 'viewName': 'List' },
            'detail': { 'viewName': 'Detail' },
            'edit': { 'viewName': 'Edit' }
        }
    }
}
```

## Component.js
```javascript
sap.ui.define([
    'sap/ui/core/UIComponent'
], function(UIComponent) {
    return UIComponent.extend('com.empresa.miapp.Component', {
        metadata: { manifest: 'json' },
        init: function() {
            UIComponent.prototype.init.apply(this, arguments);
            this.getRouter().initialize();
        }
    });
});
```

## Navigate en controller
```javascript
this.getOwnerComponent().getRouter().navTo('detail', {
    productId: '123'
});
```

## Ver current route params
```javascript
var oRouter = this.getOwnerComponent().getRouter();
oRouter.attachRoutePatternMatched(function(oEvent) {
    if (oEvent.getParameter('name') === 'detail') {
        var oArgs = oEvent.getParameter('arguments');
        var productId = oArgs.productId;
        // Load data for productId
    }
});
```

## Multiple pattern
Same view for different URL structures:
```json
{ 'pattern': 'products', 'name': 'list', 'target': 'list' },
{ 'pattern': 'products/', 'name': 'list2', 'target': 'list' }
```

## Query parameters
Patterns don't include query params, but they're accessible:
```javascript
var oQuery = new URLSearchParams(window.location.hash.split('?')[1]);
var filter = oQuery.get('filter');
```

## Master-Detail layout
### Split app pattern
```xml
<SplitApp id='app'>
    <masterPages/>
    <detailPages/>
</SplitApp>
```

### Routing
```json
'controlAggregation': 'masterPages'   // for master target
'controlAggregation': 'detailPages'   // for detail target
```

## Back navigation
```javascript
var oHistory = sap.ui.core.routing.History.getInstance();
var sPreviousHash = oHistory.getPreviousHash();
if (sPreviousHash) {
    window.history.go(-1);
} else {
    this.getOwnerComponent().getRouter().navTo('list', {}, true);  // replace history
}
```

## Route not found
```json
'routes': [
    // your routes
],
'targets': {
    // your targets,
    'notFound': { 'viewName': 'NotFound' }
}
```

```javascript
// In Component init
this.getRouter().getTargets().display('notFound');
// When no route matches
```

## Deep link
Users can bookmark or share:
`https://myapp/#/detail/123`

Enter → router loads detail view con productId=123.

## Transitions
- **slide** (default)
- **fade**
- **flip**
- **show**

Apply per navigation or globally.

## sap.m.Form / SimpleForm
```xml
<SimpleForm editable='true' layout='ResponsiveGridLayout'
    labelSpanXL='2' labelSpanL='3' labelSpanM='4' labelSpanS='12'
    columnsXL='2' columnsL='2' columnsM='1' columnsS='1'>
    <Label text='Name'/>
    <Input value='{Name}' required='true'/>

    <Label text='Email'/>
    <Input value='{Email}' type='Email'/>

    <Label text='Age'/>
    <StepInput value='{Age}' min='0' max='120'/>

    <Label text='Country'/>
    <Select selectedKey='{Country}'>
        <items>
            <core:Item key='CO' text='Colombia'/>
            <core:Item key='MX' text='Mexico'/>
        </items>
    </Select>
</SimpleForm>
```

## Validation types

### Input types (native)
- `Text` (default)
- `Email`
- `Password`
- `Number`
- `Tel`
- `Url`
- `Date`

### Required
```xml
<Input value='{Name}' required='true'/>
```

Red asterisk aparece.

### Constraint validation
OData model can validate via type constraints:
```xml
<Input value='{
    path: "Price",
    type: "sap.ui.model.type.Currency",
    constraints: { minimum: 0 }
}'/>
```

### Custom validation
```javascript
_validateForm: function() {
    var oData = this.getView().getModel().getData();
    var errors = [];

    if (!oData.Name || oData.Name.length < 3) {
        errors.push({ field: 'Name', message: 'Name must be 3+ chars' });
    }
    if (oData.Email && !/^\S+@\S+\.\S+$/.test(oData.Email)) {
        errors.push({ field: 'Email', message: 'Invalid email' });
    }

    return errors;
},

onSave: function() {
    var errors = this._validateForm();
    if (errors.length) {
        sap.m.MessageToast.show(errors[0].message);
        return;
    }
    // Proceed with save
}
```

## Message manager
Centralized message handling:
```javascript
var oMessageManager = sap.ui.getCore().getMessageManager();

// Enable auto validation
oMessageManager.registerObject(oInput, true);

// Show message toast
sap.m.MessageToast.show('Saved successfully');

// Show dialog
sap.m.MessageBox.error('Save failed: DB error');

// Add persistent message
oMessageManager.addMessages(new sap.ui.core.message.Message({
    message: 'Invalid input',
    type: sap.ui.core.MessageType.Error,
    target: '/Name'
}));
```

## MessagePopover
```xml
<Button icon='sap-icon://message-popup' press='.onMessagesPress'/>
```

```javascript
onMessagesPress: function() {
    var oMessagesPopover = new sap.m.MessagePopover({
        items: {
            path: 'message>/',
            template: new sap.m.MessagePopoverItem({
                title: '{message>message}',
                type: '{message>type}'
            })
        }
    });
    oMessagesPopover.openBy(this.byId('messageButton'));
}
```

## Dirty flag
Track unsaved changes:
```javascript
var oModel = this.getView().getModel();
var bDirty = oModel.hasPendingChanges();

window.addEventListener('beforeunload', (e) => {
    if (oModel.hasPendingChanges()) {
        e.preventDefault();
        return 'Unsaved changes will be lost';
    }
});
```

## Two-way binding y auto-submit
OData v4 con `AutoSubmit` mode:
- User types → change tracked
- After X seconds idle → auto-submitted

O manual:
```javascript
oModel.submitBatch('mainGroup');
```

## Common patterns
- **Save + Cancel buttons**
- **Undo/Redo** (advanced)
- **Field-level errors** con `valueState`
- **Section validation** — validate as user completes each section

## valueState
```xml
<Input value='{Email}' valueState='Error' valueStateText='Invalid email'/>
```

### States
- **None**
- **Success**
- **Warning**
- **Error**
- **Information**

## Dialog
Modal window blocking main UI.

### Definition (XML fragment)
```xml
<Dialog title='Confirm' contentWidth='400px'>
    <content>
        <Text text='Delete this item?'/>
    </content>
    <beginButton>
        <Button text='Delete' type='Reject' press='.onConfirm'/>
    </beginButton>
    <endButton>
        <Button text='Cancel' press='.onCancel'/>
    </endButton>
</Dialog>
```

### Load + open
```javascript
_confirmDialog: null,

onDeletePress: function() {
    if (!this._confirmDialog) {
        sap.ui.core.Fragment.load({
            name: 'com.empresa.miapp.fragment.ConfirmDialog',
            controller: this
        }).then((oDialog) => {
            this._confirmDialog = oDialog;
            this.getView().addDependent(oDialog);
            oDialog.open();
        });
    } else {
        this._confirmDialog.open();
    }
},

onConfirm: function() {
    // Perform delete
    this._confirmDialog.close();
},

onCancel: function() {
    this._confirmDialog.close();
}
```

## Popover
Non-modal (user can click outside to close).

```xml
<Popover title='Filter'>
    <content>
        <Input placeholder='Search...'/>
    </content>
</Popover>
```

### Open near button
```javascript
onFilterPress: function(oEvent) {
    sap.ui.core.Fragment.load({...}).then((oPopover) => {
        oPopover.openBy(oEvent.getSource());
    });
}
```

## MessageBox (quick alerts)
```javascript
sap.m.MessageBox.confirm('Delete item?', {
    onClose: (sAction) => {
        if (sAction === sap.m.MessageBox.Action.OK) {
            // Delete
        }
    }
});

sap.m.MessageBox.error('Failed: ...');
sap.m.MessageBox.warning('Are you sure?');
sap.m.MessageBox.information('Info message');
sap.m.MessageBox.success('Saved!');
```

## MessageToast (transient)
```javascript
sap.m.MessageToast.show('Item saved', { duration: 3000 });
```

Disappears automatically.

## Busy indicator
```javascript
sap.ui.core.BusyIndicator.show(0);   // 0 delay
// Long operation
sap.ui.core.BusyIndicator.hide();
```

Or on specific control:
```javascript
this.getView().setBusy(true);
```

## SelectDialog
Select from list dialog (like a chooser):
```xml
<SelectDialog title='Select Product' items='{/Products}' confirm='.onProductSelected'>
    <StandardListItem title='{Name}' description='{Category}'/>
</SelectDialog>
```

```javascript
onProductSelected: function(oEvent) {
    var oSelected = oEvent.getParameter('selectedItem');
    // Handle
}
```

## ViewSettingsDialog
Table filter/sort/group dialog:
```xml
<ViewSettingsDialog confirm='.onSortConfirm'>
    <sortItems>
        <ViewSettingsItem text='Name' key='Name'/>
        <ViewSettingsItem text='Price' key='Price'/>
    </sortItems>
</ViewSettingsDialog>
```

## Best practices
- **Load fragments lazily** (only when opened first time)
- **addDependent** so dialog cleans up with view
- **Destroy** dialog if not reused frequently
- **Focus management** — focus first input on open
